# THE D8R FILE IS FROZEN BEHIND A GRADED TWO-ROW PASS AND IS NOT EDITED BY THIS ITEM.
# This diff is the supervisor's reading path (SUPERVISION_CHARTER.md section 3, check 1).
#
# The hunks fall in six classes:
#
#   (a) INHERITED IN SHAPE, and visible as context: the pidfile and the
#       two-records-for-one-run refusal, ALREADY_BOUGHT, the windowed H5 gate, the AGGREGATE
#       and G-CPUSET wait-and-retry guards with their series files, STATUS.<arm>, the
#       CHAIN_DONE trap (D5 Addendum 3 A3.5), the per-arm image selection (*-P patched,
#       *-S shipped, PATCHED FIRST) and the frozen comparator at chain end whose rc is
#       INFRASTRUCTURE (L-342) and never the verdict.
#
#   (b) NEW: THE G-FREEZE.0 TOKEN GUARD, lifted in form from d8g_run_arm.sh -- the
#       two-halves pattern so the guard's own lines do not match it, and the PLANTED
#       SENTINEL so a grep that can see nothing cannot report zero.  THE DRIVER IS
#       FAIL-CLOSED AND WAS DEMONSTRATED TO BE: run as a draft it exits 3 and names all six
#       placeholders.  D8R's driver had no such guard because D8R's constants all existed.
#
#   (c) TEN ARMS, NOT FOUR, AND A PREREQUISITE GATE.  F2-P requires an rc=0 ledger row for
#       A2-P AND the file A2-P/d8g_A.json (F2-S likewise for A2-S), because the FD table
#       must stand beside ITS OWN ROW's adjoint -- the comparator refuses on
#       adjoint_source.md5 != md5(<dep>/d8g_A.json).  The launcher checks this too, but only
#       AFTER the driver's 60 s H5 window and a possibly four-hour aggregate wait.  Here it
#       is checked FIRST, so a mis-ordered chain costs a second rather than an hour.
#
#   (d) THE DRIVER STAGES NO MESH AND GENERATES NONE.  D8R copied ONE frozen base/ tree from
#       D8's run root and md5-asserted 23 input files.  D8G has THREE meshes that do not
#       exist until d8g_genmesh.sh builds them, and mesh generation is a SEPARATELY COSTED
#       step (section 6.3: 9.000 core-min, L3 measured at 4.183) that writes the very
#       construction record the comparator's G-MESH / G-SYS / G-BODY / G-TE read.  A driver
#       that generated it would make the geometry a side effect of the chain that consumes
#       it.  So the three level bases and the three mesh records are REQUIRED, the driver
#       REFUSES if any is absent, and it prints the three genmesh commands.
#
#   (e) TWO DIFFERENT KINDS OF CLAIM PER LEVEL, AND THEY ARE LABELLED AS SUCH.
#       - `cells` in the mesh record is asserted against section 2.2's REGISTERED integers
#         (5,568 / 44,544 / 356,352).  That is a FROZEN CONSTANT and a mismatch aborts.
#       - `points_md5` is NOT registered and CANNOT BE: re-coarsening is not byte-reproducible
