#         driver asserts is SELF-CONSISTENCY -- that base_<LEVEL>/constant/polyMesh/points.gz
#         hashes to the value its own record claims.  The arm-side binding is the
#         comparator's G-M2, which hashes every arm's points.gz against the same record.
#       D8R needed neither distinction: its one mesh was a frozen input with a frozen md5.
#
#   (f) SECTION 5's THREE-TIER MEMORY TABLE replaces D8R's two-tier one: L1/L2 primal
#       6 GiB cap / H5 floor 8.0; L3 primal 12 GiB / 14.0; the L2 adjoint and FD arms
#       14 GiB / 16.0 (cap + 2 GiB, per the section 5 headroom column, not D8R's +4 rule --
#       the numbers come from the registered table, not from a carried-over formula).
#       L3 ADJOINT IS NOT AN ARM OF THIS ITEM and cannot be named to this driver at all
#       (section 7: BLOCKED on memory AND, independently, on conditioning).
#
# THE ONE md5 THIS FILE ASSERTS AS A REAL VALUE IS MD5_DECOMP = 1dbd9ead3f40a29f483444dc5fa1288b,
# and it is not a guess: d8g_decomposeParDict.DRAFT is a BYTE COPY of the FROZEN, GRADED
# curriculum_D8R/d8r_decomposeParDict, and the lane that wrote that line verified both files
# hash to it.  See d8g_decomposeParDict_DELTAS_from_d8r.diff -- which is EMPTY, deliberately.
#
# NOT TESTED, STATED PLAINLY: this driver has never been run past its own freeze guard,
